# AppHelpGuides -- what does not belong in the repository.
#
# The repository holds the finished guides and the scripts that make them.
# It does not hold harvests: those are raw copies of other people's help
# centres, they run to hundreds of megabytes, and they can be regathered by
# running the script again.

# Harvest folders, which the get<Name>Help.py scripts create beside themselves.
*Help/
*HelpSmall/
ZoomHelpSmall*/

# Harvest archives and their shrunk parts. The finished guide archives, which
# are named <Name>_Help_Guide.zip, are kept -- the rule below re-admits them.
*Help.zip
*HelpSmall*.zip
*Transcripts.zip
!*_Help_Guide.zip
!*_User_Guide.zip

# Run logs. The logs matter while diagnosing a run, not afterwards.
*.cmd
*.ps1
temp.txt
*.md
*.log

# Python and editor leavings.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Windows and archive tool leavings.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp
~$*

# Harvested pages holding sample credentials, which GitHub blocks.
GitHub.htm
